{# The layout of the pages of the bundle, overridden by the application to give them their look
   (architecture §5.2, §6): the same blocks as the layout of the bundle, filled by one of the two skeletons
   of layout/, which carry the document, the one stylesheet and no script. The pages of the bundle come with
   it untouched: what they render is styled by its structure and its data-* codes.

   Which skeleton a page is served in, is its route (architecture §5.4). A page of an interaction asks one
   thing of whoever is in front of it and has nothing else on it; a page of the account is a page someone
   reads and comes back to. Everything that follows from that is in the skeleton, and nothing of it here. #}
{% extends (app.request.attributes.get('_route') ?? '') starts with 'beffroi_interaction_account'
    ? 'layout/account.html.twig'
    : 'layout/interaction.html.twig' %}
